<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:zeebe="http://camunda.org/schema/zeebe/1.0" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" xmlns:bioc="http://bpmn.io/schema/bpmn/biocolor/1.0" xmlns:color="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/non-normative/color/1.0" xmlns:modeler="http://camunda.org/schema/modeler/1.0" id="Definitions_1brddg4" targetNamespace="http://bpmn.io/schema/bpmn" exporter="Camunda Modeler" exporterVersion="5.51.1" modeler:executionPlatform="Camunda Cloud" modeler:executionPlatformVersion="8.10.0">
  <bpmn:collaboration id="Collaboration_0t0nskd">
    <bpmn:documentation>Two agents in one process instance that talk Agent-to-Agent (A2A) 1.0 over HTTP. The client agent is the main flow. The server agent lives in event sub-processes that the client's A2A calls trigger: the agent query parameter in the URLs finds this instance, and the taskId finds a waiting task.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:participant id="Participant_Agents" name="A2A agents (one process instance)" processRef="a2a-two-agents" />
    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="Note_ServerRole">
      <bpmn:text>Server agent, in the same instance as the client. Its two event sub-processes (non-interrupting) are triggered only by the client's A2A calls: the A2A 1.0 Server templates (on the OOTB HTTP webhook) take the agent query parameter of the Agent Card and JSON-RPC URLs as correlation key, so each call finds this instance. Each A2A task runs in its own event sub-process instance; its end event ends the task, not the instance.</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="Note_FetchAgentCard">
      <bpmn:text>Discovery (A2A 1.0 Client template, fetchAgentCard). Replaces the example's MCP 'List resources' step. Reads the remote agent's Agent Card (name, description, skills, JSON-RPC interface).</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="Note_ClientAgent">
      <bpmn:text>Same AI agent and chat loop as the MCP-resources example. New tool: 'Ask remote agent' (A2A 1.0 Client template, sendMessage). The LLM writes the message with fromAi() and passes the taskId back when the remote agent asked for more input.</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="Note_RemoteAgentReplied">
      <bpmn:text>Correlated message event (A2A 1.0 Client Webhook template): the key is the task ID on both sides, and the X-A2A-Notification-Token header must match the A2A_PUSH_TOKEN secret. It fires on final, input-required and auth-required states; the pushed Task becomes toolCallResult.</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="Note_Push">
      <bpmn:text>Push notification: POST of an A2A 1.0 StreamResponse ({task}) to the client's webhook URL with the X-A2A-Notification-Token header. The agent picks state and text with fromAi(); input-required waits here for the client's answer.</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn:association id="Assoc_FetchAgentCard" associationDirection="None" sourceRef="Client_FetchAgentCard" targetRef="Note_FetchAgentCard" />
    <bpmn:association id="Assoc_ClientAgent" associationDirection="None" sourceRef="Client_AI_Agent" targetRef="Note_ClientAgent" />
    <bpmn:association id="Assoc_RemoteAgentReplied" associationDirection="None" sourceRef="Tool_RemoteAgentReplied" targetRef="Note_RemoteAgentReplied" />
    <bpmn:association id="Assoc_ServerRole" associationDirection="None" sourceRef="Server_MessageReceived" targetRef="Note_ServerRole" />
    <bpmn:association id="Assoc_Push" associationDirection="None" sourceRef="Server_PushNotification" targetRef="Note_Push" />
  </bpmn:collaboration>
  <bpmn:process id="a2a-two-agents" name="A2A two agents" isExecutable="true">
    <bpmn:laneSet id="LaneSet_Agents">
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Client" name="Client agent (A2A client)">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Client_Start</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Client_FetchAgentCard</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Client_JoinGateway</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Client_AI_Agent</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Client_UserFeedback</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Client_UserSatisfied</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Client_End</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Server" name="Server agent (A2A server)">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Activity_1mwggyd</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Activity_0u82j95</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
    </bpmn:laneSet>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="Client_Start" name="Request received">
      <bpmn:documentation>Starts the conversation, and with it the server agent: both agents live in this instance. a2aAgentId is the ID the server agent is reached by; the client puts it in the Agent Card URL.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <zeebe:formDefinition formId="ai-agent-chat-mcp-resources-initial-request" />
        <zeebe:ioMapping>
          <zeebe:output source="=string(uuid())" target="a2aAgentId" />
        </zeebe:ioMapping>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_C1</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Client_FetchAgentCard" name="Fetch remote agent card" zeebe:modelerTemplate="dev.hansel.a2a.client.v1" zeebe:modelerTemplateVersion="1" zeebe:modelerTemplateIcon="data:image/svg+xml;base64,">
      <bpmn:documentation>A2A 1.0 Client, operation fetchAgentCard. Reads the remote agent's Agent Card and stores it in remoteAgentCard, which the client agent's system prompt includes and the Ask remote agent tool takes its JSON-RPC URL from.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <zeebe:taskDefinition type="io.camunda:http-json:1" retries="3" />
        <zeebe:ioMapping>
          <zeebe:input source="{{secrets.A2A_CONNECTORS_URL}}/inbound" target="baseUrl" />
          <zeebe:input source="noAuth" target="authType" />
          <zeebe:input source="noAuth" target="authentication.type" />
          <zeebe:input source="fetchAgentCard" target="operationId" />
          <zeebe:input source="=&#34;a2a-server-card?agent=&#34; + a2aAgentId" target="agentCardLocation" />
          <zeebe:input source="=&#34;/&#34;+agentCardLocation" target="operationPath" />
          <zeebe:input source="={&#34;A2A-Version&#34;: &#34;1.0&#34;}" target="headers" />
          <zeebe:input source="={}" target="queryParameters" />
          <zeebe:input source="GET" target="method" />
          <zeebe:input source="=true" target="ignoreNullValues" />
          <zeebe:input source="=if operationId = &#34;sendMessage&#34; and rpcUrl != null then rpcUrl else baseUrl + operationPath" target="url" />
        </zeebe:ioMapping>
        <zeebe:taskHeaders>
          <zeebe:header key="resultExpression" value="={remoteAgentCard: {result: response.body}}" />
          <zeebe:header key="retryBackoff" value="PT30S" />
        </zeebe:taskHeaders>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_C1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_C2</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Client_JoinGateway">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_C2</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_C7</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_C3</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:userTask id="Client_UserFeedback" name="User feedback">
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <zeebe:userTask />
        <zeebe:formDefinition formId="ai-agent-chat-mcp-resources-user-feedback" />
        <zeebe:ioMapping>
          <zeebe:input source="=agent.responseText" target="responseText" />
        </zeebe:ioMapping>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_C4</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_C5</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:userTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Client_UserSatisfied" name="User satisfied?">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_C5</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_C7</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_C6</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="Client_End" name="Request answered">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_C6</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:adHocSubProcess id="Client_AI_Agent" name="Client AI agent" zeebe:modelerTemplate="io.camunda.connectors.agenticai.ai-agent-subprocess.v2" zeebe:modelerTemplateVersion="1" zeebe:modelerTemplateIcon="data:image/svg+xml;base64,">
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <zeebe:adHoc outputCollection="toolCallResults" outputElement="={&#10;  id: toolCall._meta.id,&#10;  name: toolCall._meta.name,&#10;  content: toolCallResult,&#10;  completedAt: now()&#10;}" />
        <zeebe:taskDefinition type="io.camunda.agenticai:aiagent:subprocess:2" retries="3" />
        <zeebe:ioMapping>
          <zeebe:input source="openai" target="provider.type" />
          <zeebe:input source="completions" target="provider.openai.api.type" />
          <zeebe:input source="custom" target="provider.openai.backend.type" />
          <zeebe:input source="{{secrets.CAMUNDA_PROVIDED_LLM_API_ENDPOINT}}" target="provider.openai.backend.custom.endpoint" />
          <zeebe:input source="apiKey" target="provider.openai.backend.custom.authentication.type" />
          <zeebe:input source="{{secrets.CAMUNDA_PROVIDED_LLM_API_KEY}}" target="provider.openai.backend.custom.authentication.apiKey" />
          <zeebe:input source="PT180S" target="provider.openai.timeouts.timeout" />
          <zeebe:input source="{{secrets.CAMUNDA_PROVIDED_LLM_DEFAULT_MODEL}}" target="provider.openai.model.model" />
          <zeebe:input source="modelDefault" target="provider.openai.api.completions.effort" />
          <zeebe:input source="=&#34;You are a helpful assistant. Answer each request from these sources, in this order:&#10;&#10;1. Your own tools. Use every tool that fits the request, as often as needed. Never invent a tool. Never guess contact details: look people up with the user tools.&#10;2. The remote agent, through Tool_AskRemoteAgent. Use it when none of your tools fits the request, or when your tools fail or find nothing.&#10;3. Your own knowledge. Use it only when neither your tools nor the remote agent can answer, and say that the answer is a best-effort guess.&#10;&#10;If the remote agent asks a question that the conversation does not answer, ask the user.&#10;&#10;The remote agent: &#34; + string({name: remoteAgentCard.result.name, description: remoteAgentCard.result.description, skills: remoteAgentCard.result.skills})" target="data.systemPrompt.prompt" />
          <zeebe:input source="=if (is defined(followUpInput)) then followUpInput else inputText" target="data.userPrompt.prompt" />
          <zeebe:input source="=agent.context" target="agentContext" />
          <zeebe:input source="in-process" target="data.memory.storage.type" />
          <zeebe:input source="=20" target="data.memory.contextWindowSize" />
          <zeebe:input source="=20" target="data.limits.maxModelCalls" />
          <zeebe:input source="WAIT_FOR_TOOL_CALL_RESULTS" target="data.events.behavior" />
          <zeebe:input source="text" target="data.response.format.type" />
          <zeebe:input source="=false" target="data.response.format.parseJson" />
          <zeebe:input source="=false" target="data.response.includeAssistantMessage" />
          <zeebe:input source="=true" target="data.response.includeAgentContext" />
          <zeebe:input target="agent" />
          <zeebe:output source="=agent" target="agent" />
        </zeebe:ioMapping>
        <zeebe:taskHeaders>
          <zeebe:header key="elementTemplateVersion" value="1" />
          <zeebe:header key="elementTemplateId" value="io.camunda.connectors.agenticai.ai-agent-subprocess.v2" />
          <zeebe:header key="retryBackoff" value="PT30S" />
        </zeebe:taskHeaders>
        <zeebe:properties>
          <zeebe:property name="io.camunda.agenticai.toolContainer" value="true" />
        </zeebe:properties>
        <zeebe:agentDefinition agentType="aiAgentSubProcess" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_C3</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_C4</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="Tool_ListUsers" name="List users" zeebe:modelerTemplate="io.camunda.connectors.HttpJson.v2" zeebe:modelerTemplateVersion="18" zeebe:modelerTemplateIcon="data:image/svg+xml;base64,">
        <bpmn:documentation>Lists all available users. More contact details (such as e-mail addresses) can be loaded up by looking up the individual user by ID.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:extensionElements>
          <zeebe:taskDefinition type="io.camunda:http-json:1" retries="3" />
          <zeebe:ioMapping>
            <zeebe:input source="noAuth" target="authentication.type" />
            <zeebe:input source="GET" target="method" />
            <zeebe:input source="https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/users" target="url" />
            <zeebe:input source="=false" target="followRedirects" />
            <zeebe:input source="JSON" target="documentReturnFormat.choice" />
            <zeebe:input source="20" target="connectionTimeoutInSeconds" />
            <zeebe:input source="20" target="readTimeoutInSeconds" />
          </zeebe:ioMapping>
          <zeebe:taskHeaders>
            <zeebe:header key="elementTemplateVersion" value="18" />
            <zeebe:header key="elementTemplateId" value="io.camunda.connectors.HttpJson.v2" />
            <zeebe:header key="resultExpression" value="={&#10;  toolCallResult: for user in response.body return {&#10;    id: user.id,&#10;    name: user.name,&#10;    username: user.username&#10;  }&#10;}" />
            <zeebe:header key="retryBackoff" value="PT30S" />
          </zeebe:taskHeaders>
        </bpmn:extensionElements>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="Tool_LoadUserByID" name="Load user by ID" zeebe:modelerTemplate="io.camunda.connectors.HttpJson.v2" zeebe:modelerTemplateVersion="18" zeebe:modelerTemplateIcon="data:image/svg+xml;base64,">
        <bpmn:documentation>Loads a user by ID</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:extensionElements>
          <zeebe:taskDefinition type="io.camunda:http-json:1" retries="0" />
          <zeebe:ioMapping>
            <zeebe:input source="noAuth" target="authentication.type" />
            <zeebe:input source="GET" target="method" />
            <zeebe:input source="=&#34;https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/users/&#34; + string(fromAi(toolCall.id, &#34;The user ID&#34;, &#34;number&#34;))" target="url" />
            <zeebe:input source="=false" target="followRedirects" />
            <zeebe:input source="JSON" target="documentReturnFormat.choice" />
            <zeebe:input source="20" target="connectionTimeoutInSeconds" />
            <zeebe:input source="20" target="readTimeoutInSeconds" />
          </zeebe:ioMapping>
          <zeebe:taskHeaders>
            <zeebe:header key="elementTemplateVersion" value="18" />
            <zeebe:header key="elementTemplateId" value="io.camunda.connectors.HttpJson.v2" />
            <zeebe:header key="resultExpression" value="={&#10;  toolCallResult: if (is defined(response.body.id)) then response.body else &#34;User not found&#34;&#10;}" />
            <zeebe:header key="retryBackoff" value="PT30S" />
          </zeebe:taskHeaders>
        </bpmn:extensionElements>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="Tool_AskHumanToSendEmail" name="Ask human to send email">
        <bpmn:documentation>Ask a human to send an email for you</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:extensionElements>
          <zeebe:userTask />
          <zeebe:formDefinition formId="ai-agent-chat-human-send-email-request" />
          <zeebe:ioMapping>
            <zeebe:input source="=fromAi(toolCall.instructions, &#34;Instructions for the human to follow when sending the email, including background of the email.&#34;)" target="instructions" />
            <zeebe:input source="=fromAi(toolCall.recipient_name, &#34;The recipient&#39;s full name.&#34;)" target="recipient_name" />
            <zeebe:input source="=fromAi(toolCall.recipient_email, &#34;The the recipient&#39;s email address.&#34;)" target="recipient_email" />
            <zeebe:input source="=fromAi(toolCall.email_subject, &#34;The subject of the email.&#34;)" target="email_subject" />
            <zeebe:input source="=fromAi(toolCall.email_body, &#34;The body of the email.&#34;)" target="email_body" />
            <zeebe:output source="={&#10;  operatorFeedback: operatorFeedback,&#10;  emailOk: emailOk&#10;}" target="toolCallResult" />
          </zeebe:ioMapping>
        </bpmn:extensionElements>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="Tool_AskRemoteAgent" name="Ask remote agent" zeebe:modelerTemplate="dev.hansel.a2a.client.v1" zeebe:modelerTemplateVersion="1" zeebe:modelerTemplateIcon="data:image/svg+xml;base64,">
        <bpmn:documentation>Send a message to the remote A2A agent described in your system prompt. Use it for requests that match its skills. If it answered with TASK_STATE_INPUT_REQUIRED, call this tool again with its taskId and contextId and the answer to its question. A task in any other final state (completed, failed, canceled) is closed: leave taskId out to start a new task. The result arrives as a push notification.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:extensionElements>
          <zeebe:taskDefinition type="io.camunda:http-json:1" retries="3" />
          <zeebe:ioMapping>
            <zeebe:input source="{{secrets.A2A_CONNECTORS_URL}}/inbound" target="baseUrl" />
            <zeebe:input source="noAuth" target="authType" />
            <zeebe:input source="noAuth" target="authentication.type" />
            <zeebe:input source="sendMessage" target="operationId" />
            <zeebe:input source="a2a" target="rpcPath" />
            <zeebe:input source="=&#34;/&#34;+rpcPath" target="operationPath" />
            <zeebe:input source="={&#34;A2A-Version&#34;: &#34;1.0&#34;, &#34;Content-Type&#34;: &#34;application/json&#34;}" target="headers" />
            <zeebe:input source="={}" target="queryParameters" />
            <zeebe:input source="POST" target="method" />
            <zeebe:input source="=fromAi(toolCall.text, &#34;The message for the remote agent. When it asked for more input, this is the answer.&#34;)" target="text" />
            <zeebe:input source="=fromAi(value: toolCall.taskId, description: &#34;The task ID of a remote task in TASK_STATE_INPUT_REQUIRED that this message answers. Leave it out for a new request.&#34;, type: &#34;string&#34;, options: {required: false})" target="taskId" />
            <zeebe:input source="=fromAi(value: toolCall.contextId, description: &#34;The context ID of that remote task. Leave it out for a new request.&#34;, type: &#34;string&#34;, options: {required: false})" target="contextId" />
            <zeebe:input source="{{secrets.A2A_CONNECTORS_URL}}/inbound/a2a-client-agent-reply" target="webhookUrl" />
            <zeebe:input source="{{secrets.A2A_PUSH_TOKEN}}" target="pushToken" />
            <zeebe:input source="={jsonrpc: &#34;2.0&#34;, id: string(uuid()), method: &#34;SendMessage&#34;, params: { message: {messageId: string(uuid()), role: &#34;ROLE_USER&#34;, parts: [{text: text}], taskId: taskId, contextId: contextId}, configuration: { returnImmediately: webhookUrl != null, taskPushNotificationConfig: if webhookUrl != null then {url: webhookUrl, token: pushToken} else null}}}" target="body" />
            <zeebe:input source="=(remoteAgentCard.result.supportedInterfaces[item.protocolBinding = &#34;JSONRPC&#34;])[1].url" target="rpcUrl" />
            <zeebe:input source="=true" target="ignoreNullValues" />
            <zeebe:input source="=if operationId = &#34;sendMessage&#34; and rpcUrl != null then rpcUrl else baseUrl + operationPath" target="url" />
          </zeebe:ioMapping>
          <zeebe:taskHeaders>
            <zeebe:header key="resultExpression" value="={agentResponse: { result: if response.body.result.task != null then response.body.result.task else if response.body.result.message != null then response.body.result.message else if response.body.result = null and response.body.error = null then response.body else null, error: response.body.error}}" />
            <zeebe:header key="retryBackoff" value="PT30S" />
          </zeebe:taskHeaders>
        </bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_T1</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:intermediateCatchEvent id="Tool_RemoteAgentReplied" name="Remote agent replied" zeebe:modelerTemplate="dev.hansel.a2a.client.webhook.intermediate.v1" zeebe:modelerTemplateVersion="1" zeebe:modelerTemplateIcon="data:image/svg+xml;base64,">
        <bpmn:documentation>Correlated intermediate message catch event (A2A Client Webhook connector). The subscription key is the task ID from the client response plus '-' plus the notification token. The inbound webhook computes the same key from the push request (body id + X-A2A-Notification-Token header), so the reply reaches exactly this tool call. It activates only when the task state is final; the Task becomes toolCallResult for the AI agent.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:extensionElements>
          <zeebe:properties>
            <zeebe:property name="inbound.type" value="io.camunda:webhook:1" />
            <zeebe:property name="inbound.shouldValidateHmac" value="disabled" />
            <zeebe:property name="synchronousResponse" value="false" />
            <zeebe:property name="consumeUnmatchedEvents" value="true" />
            <zeebe:property name="deduplicationModeManualFlag" value="false" />
            <zeebe:property name="deduplicationMode" value="AUTO" />
            <zeebe:property name="inbound.method" value="post" />
            <zeebe:property name="inbound.context" value="a2a-client-agent-reply" />
            <zeebe:property name="inbound.auth.type" value="APIKEY" />
            <zeebe:property name="inbound.auth.apiKey" value="{{secrets.A2A_PUSH_TOKEN}}" />
            <zeebe:property name="inbound.auth.apiKeyLocator" value="=request.headers.`x-a2a-notification-token`" />
            <zeebe:property name="correlationKeyExpression" value="=(if request.body.task != null then request.body.task.id else request.body.statusUpdate.taskId)" />
            <zeebe:property name="activationCondition" value="=list contains([&#34;TASK_STATE_COMPLETED&#34;, &#34;TASK_STATE_FAILED&#34;, &#34;TASK_STATE_CANCELED&#34;, &#34;TASK_STATE_REJECTED&#34;, &#34;TASK_STATE_INPUT_REQUIRED&#34;, &#34;TASK_STATE_AUTH_REQUIRED&#34;], (if request.body.task != null then request.body.task.status.state else request.body.statusUpdate.status.state))" />
            <zeebe:property name="resultExpression" value="={toolCallResult: if request.body.task != null then request.body.task else request.body}" />
          </zeebe:properties>
        </bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bpmn:incoming>Flow_T1</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:messageEventDefinition id="MessageEventDefinition_0y3ixuv" messageRef="Message_0g0kguo" />
      </bpmn:intermediateCatchEvent>
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_T1" sourceRef="Tool_AskRemoteAgent" targetRef="Tool_RemoteAgentReplied" />
    </bpmn:adHocSubProcess>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_C1" sourceRef="Client_Start" targetRef="Client_FetchAgentCard" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_C2" sourceRef="Client_FetchAgentCard" targetRef="Client_JoinGateway" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_C7" name="no - we follow up" sourceRef="Client_UserSatisfied" targetRef="Client_JoinGateway">
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">=userSatisfied = null or userSatisfied = false</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_C3" sourceRef="Client_JoinGateway" targetRef="Client_AI_Agent" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_C4" sourceRef="Client_AI_Agent" targetRef="Client_UserFeedback" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_C5" sourceRef="Client_UserFeedback" targetRef="Client_UserSatisfied" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_C6" name="yes" sourceRef="Client_UserSatisfied" targetRef="Client_End">
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">=userSatisfied</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:subProcess id="Activity_1mwggyd" name="GET Agent Card" triggeredByEvent="true">
      <bpmn:startEvent id="Server_CardRequested" name="Agent Card requested" zeebe:modelerTemplate="dev.hansel.a2a.server.card.v1" zeebe:modelerTemplateVersion="2" zeebe:modelerTemplateIcon="data:image/svg+xml;base64," isInterrupting="false">
        <bpmn:extensionElements>
          <zeebe:properties>
            <zeebe:property name="inbound.type" value="io.camunda:webhook:1" />
            <zeebe:property name="inbound.shouldValidateHmac" value="disabled" />
            <zeebe:property name="inbound.auth.type" value="NONE" />
            <zeebe:property name="synchronousResponse" value="false" />
            <zeebe:property name="consumeUnmatchedEvents" value="true" />
            <zeebe:property name="deduplicationModeManualFlag" value="false" />
            <zeebe:property name="deduplicationMode" value="AUTO" />
            <zeebe:property name="inbound.method" value="get" />
            <zeebe:property name="inbound.context" value="a2a-server-card" />
            <zeebe:property name="resultExpression" value="={}" />
            <zeebe:property name="correlationRequired" value="required" />
            <zeebe:property name="correlationKeyExpression" value="=request.params.agent" />
            <zeebe:property name="inbound.responseExpression" value="={card: { name: &#34;Task agent&#34;, description: &#34;Converts temperatures, lists tech stuff and answers general questions. Asks for clarification when a request is ambiguous.&#34;, version: &#34;1.0.0&#34;, skills: [{id: &#34;convert-temperature&#34;, name: &#34;Convert a temperature&#34;, description: &#34;Converts a temperature between celsius, fahrenheit and kelvin.&#34;, tags: [&#34;temperature&#34;, &#34;units&#34;]}, {id: &#34;list-tech-stuff&#34;, name: &#34;List tech stuff&#34;, description: &#34;Lists all available tech stuff.&#34;, tags: [&#34;inventory&#34;]}, {id: &#34;answer&#34;, name: &#34;Answer a question&#34;, description: &#34;Answers general questions and asks for clarification when a request is ambiguous.&#34;, tags: [&#34;qa&#34;]}]}, response: {statusCode: 200, headers: {&#34;Content-Type&#34;: &#34;application/json&#34;}, body: context merge([card, { supportedInterfaces: [{url: &#34;{{secrets.A2A_CONNECTORS_URL}}/inbound/a2a-server?agent=&#34; + request.params.agent, protocolBinding: &#34;JSONRPC&#34;, protocolVersion: &#34;1.0&#34;}], capabilities: {streaming: false, pushNotifications: true, extendedAgentCard: false}, defaultInputModes: [&#34;text/plain&#34;], defaultOutputModes: [&#34;text/plain&#34;]}])} }.response" />
          </zeebe:properties>
        </bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_0axxcf7</bpmn:outgoing>
        <bpmn:messageEventDefinition id="MessageEventDefinition_0jssx10" messageRef="Message_1exsyfd" />
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_0axxcf7" sourceRef="Server_CardRequested" targetRef="Server_CardServed" />
      <bpmn:endEvent id="Server_CardServed" name="Card served">
        <bpmn:incoming>Flow_0axxcf7</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
    </bpmn:subProcess>
    <bpmn:subProcess id="Activity_0u82j95" name="A2A task" triggeredByEvent="true">
      <bpmn:documentation>One run per A2A task. The task variables are local to this run, so tasks that overlap in the same instance do not overwrite each other.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <zeebe:ioMapping>
          <zeebe:input source="=null" target="taskId" />
          <zeebe:input source="=null" target="contextId" />
          <zeebe:input source="=null" target="messageText" />
          <zeebe:input source="=null" target="pushNotification" />
          <zeebe:input source="=null" target="taskState" />
          <zeebe:input source="=null" target="serverAgent" />
        </zeebe:ioMapping>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:adHocSubProcess id="Activity_10vg0yz" name="A2A Server Agent" zeebe:modelerTemplate="io.camunda.connectors.agenticai.ai-agent-subprocess.v2-steps" zeebe:modelerTemplateVersion="1" zeebe:modelerTemplateIcon="data:image/svg+xml;base64,">
        <bpmn:extensionElements>
          <zeebe:taskDefinition type="io.camunda.agenticai:aiagent:subprocess:2" retries="3" />
          <zeebe:ioMapping>
            <zeebe:input source="openai" target="provider.type" />
            <zeebe:input source="completions" target="provider.openai.api.type" />
            <zeebe:input source="custom" target="provider.openai.backend.type" />
            <zeebe:input source="{{secrets.CAMUNDA_PROVIDED_LLM_API_ENDPOINT}}" target="provider.openai.backend.custom.endpoint" />
            <zeebe:input source="apiKey" target="provider.openai.backend.custom.authentication.type" />
            <zeebe:input source="{{secrets.CAMUNDA_PROVIDED_LLM_API_KEY}}" target="provider.openai.backend.custom.authentication.apiKey" />
            <zeebe:input source="PT180S" target="provider.openai.timeouts.timeout" />
            <zeebe:input source="{{secrets.CAMUNDA_PROVIDED_LLM_DEFAULT_MODEL}}" target="provider.openai.model.model" />
            <zeebe:input source="modelDefault" target="provider.openai.api.completions.effort" />
            <zeebe:input source="=&#34;You are TaskAgent, a remote agent that A2A clients send tasks to. Answer each task from these sources, in this order:&#10;&#10;1. Your own tools. Use every tool that fits the task. Never invent a tool.&#10;2. The client, through Server_PushNotification with TASK_STATE_INPUT_REQUIRED. Use it when the task is ambiguous, or when you need information or work that your tools cannot give.&#10;3. Your own knowledge, as a best-effort answer that you mark as such.&#10;&#10;End every task with Server_PushNotification: TASK_STATE_COMPLETED with the full answer, or TASK_STATE_FAILED with the reason.&#34;" target="data.systemPrompt.prompt" />
            <zeebe:input source="=messageText" target="data.userPrompt.prompt" />
            <zeebe:input target="agentContext" />
            <zeebe:input source="in-process" target="data.memory.storage.type" />
            <zeebe:input source="=20" target="data.memory.contextWindowSize" />
            <zeebe:input source="=10" target="data.limits.maxModelCalls" />
            <zeebe:input source="WAIT_FOR_TOOL_CALL_RESULTS" target="data.events.behavior" />
            <zeebe:input source="text" target="data.response.format.type" />
            <zeebe:input source="=false" target="data.response.format.parseJson" />
            <zeebe:input source="=false" target="data.response.includeAssistantMessage" />
            <zeebe:input source="=false" target="data.response.includeAgentContext" />
            <zeebe:input target="agent" />
            <zeebe:output source="=agent" target="serverAgent" />
          </zeebe:ioMapping>
          <zeebe:taskHeaders>
            <zeebe:header key="elementTemplateVersion" value="1" />
            <zeebe:header key="elementTemplateId" value="io.camunda.connectors.agenticai.ai-agent-subprocess.v2" />
            <zeebe:header key="retryBackoff" value="PT30S" />
          </zeebe:taskHeaders>
          <zeebe:properties>
            <zeebe:property name="io.camunda.agenticai.toolContainer" value="true" />
          </zeebe:properties>
          <zeebe:adHoc outputCollection="toolCallResults" outputElement="={&#10;  id: toolCall._meta.id,&#10;  name: toolCall._meta.name,&#10;  content: toolCallResult,&#10;  completedAt: now()&#10;}" />
          <zeebe:agentDefinition agentType="aiAgentSubProcess" />
        </bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bpmn:incoming>Flow_08f6dbl</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_1vp49c3</bpmn:outgoing>
        <bpmn:scriptTask id="Tool_ConvertTemperature" name="Convert temperature">
          <bpmn:documentation>Converts a temperature between celsius, fahrenheit and kelvin. Returns the converted value and its unit. Use it for every temperature conversion instead of calculating yourself.</bpmn:documentation>
          <bpmn:extensionElements>
            <zeebe:ioMapping>
              <zeebe:input source="=fromAi(toolCall.value, &#34;The temperature to convert&#34;, &#34;number&#34;)" target="value" />
              <zeebe:input source="=fromAi(toolCall.fromUnit, &#34;The unit of the value&#34;, &#34;string&#34;, {enum: [&#34;celsius&#34;, &#34;fahrenheit&#34;, &#34;kelvin&#34;]})" target="fromUnit" />
              <zeebe:input source="=fromAi(toolCall.toUnit, &#34;The unit to convert to&#34;, &#34;string&#34;, {enum: [&#34;celsius&#34;, &#34;fahrenheit&#34;, &#34;kelvin&#34;]})" target="toUnit" />
            </zeebe:ioMapping>
            <zeebe:script expression="={&#10;  celsius: if fromUnit = &#34;fahrenheit&#34; then (value - 32) * 5 / 9 else if fromUnit = &#34;kelvin&#34; then value - 273.15 else value,&#10;  converted: if toUnit = &#34;fahrenheit&#34; then celsius * 9 / 5 + 32 else if toUnit = &#34;kelvin&#34; then celsius + 273.15 else celsius,&#10;  result: {value: decimal(converted, 2), unit: toUnit}&#10;}.result" resultVariable="toolCallResult" />
          </bpmn:extensionElements>
        </bpmn:scriptTask>
        <bpmn:serviceTask id="Activity_0x3prgn" name="Get list of all Tech Stuff" zeebe:modelerTemplate="io.camunda.connectors.HttpJson.v2" zeebe:modelerTemplateVersion="18" zeebe:modelerTemplateIcon="data:image/svg+xml;base64,">
          <bpmn:documentation>This tool is used to get the list of all available tech stuff</bpmn:documentation>
          <bpmn:extensionElements>
            <zeebe:taskDefinition type="io.camunda:http-json:1" retries="3" />
            <zeebe:ioMapping>
              <zeebe:input source="noAuth" target="authentication.type" />
              <zeebe:input source="GET" target="method" />
              <zeebe:input source="https://api.restful-api.dev/objects" target="url" />
              <zeebe:input source="=false" target="followRedirects" />
              <zeebe:input source="JSON" target="documentReturnFormat.choice" />
              <zeebe:input source="=20" target="connectionTimeoutInSeconds" />
              <zeebe:input source="=20" target="readTimeoutInSeconds" />
            </zeebe:ioMapping>
            <zeebe:taskHeaders>
              <zeebe:header key="elementTemplateVersion" value="18" />
              <zeebe:header key="elementTemplateId" value="io.camunda.connectors.HttpJson.v2" />
              <zeebe:header key="resultExpression" value="={toolCallResult: response.body}" />
              <zeebe:header key="retryBackoff" value="PT30S" />
            </zeebe:taskHeaders>
          </bpmn:extensionElements>
        </bpmn:serviceTask>
        <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Gateway_1u02j34" name="Task state?" default="Flow_1deams4">
          <bpmn:incoming>Flow_1c5cs9r</bpmn:incoming>
          <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_1kgyvmc</bpmn:outgoing>
          <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_1deams4</bpmn:outgoing>
        </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
        <bpmn:intermediateThrowEvent id="Event_08iu22r" name="Update sent">
          <bpmn:extensionElements>
            <zeebe:ioMapping>
              <zeebe:output source="=toolCall.state" target="taskState" />
              <zeebe:output source="=&#34;Pushed &#34; + toolCall.state + &#34; to the client&#34;" target="toolCallResult" />
            </zeebe:ioMapping>
          </bpmn:extensionElements>
          <bpmn:incoming>Flow_1deams4</bpmn:incoming>
        </bpmn:intermediateThrowEvent>
        <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_1c5cs9r" sourceRef="Server_PushNotification" targetRef="Gateway_1u02j34" />
        <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_1kgyvmc" name="input-required" sourceRef="Gateway_1u02j34" targetRef="Event_1553b23">
          <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">=toolCall.state = "TASK_STATE_INPUT_REQUIRED"</bpmn:conditionExpression>
        </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
        <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_1deams4" name="other" sourceRef="Gateway_1u02j34" targetRef="Event_08iu22r" />
        <bpmn:intermediateCatchEvent id="Event_1553b23" name="A2A update received" zeebe:modelerTemplate="dev.hansel.a2a.server.send-message.follow-up.v1" zeebe:modelerTemplateVersion="1" zeebe:modelerTemplateIcon="data:image/svg+xml;base64,">
          <bpmn:documentation>A2A 1.0 Server: SendMessage (follow-up). The client's answer to the clarifying question arrives as SendMessage with this task's taskId, on the same endpoint as A2A task received; the taskId makes it land here. The answer becomes toolCallResult, and the client's new push config replaces the old one. Once the task is final nothing waits here, so the client must start a new task.</bpmn:documentation>
          <bpmn:extensionElements>
            <zeebe:properties>
              <zeebe:property name="inbound.type" value="io.camunda:webhook:1" />
              <zeebe:property name="inbound.shouldValidateHmac" value="disabled" />
              <zeebe:property name="inbound.auth.type" value="NONE" />
              <zeebe:property name="synchronousResponse" value="false" />
              <zeebe:property name="consumeUnmatchedEvents" value="true" />
              <zeebe:property name="deduplicationModeManualFlag" value="false" />
              <zeebe:property name="deduplicationMode" value="AUTO" />
              <zeebe:property name="inbound.method" value="post" />
              <zeebe:property name="inbound.context" value="a2a-server" />
              <zeebe:property name="inbound.verificationExpression" value="=if request.body.method = &#34;SendMessage&#34; and request.body.params.message.messageId != null then null else {statusCode: 200, headers: {&#34;Content-Type&#34;: &#34;application/json&#34;}, body: if request.body.method != &#34;SendMessage&#34; then {jsonrpc: &#34;2.0&#34;, id: request.body.id, error: {code: -32601, message: &#34;Method not found&#34;}} else {jsonrpc: &#34;2.0&#34;, id: request.body.id, error: {code: -32602, message: &#34;Invalid params: message.messageId is required&#34;}}}" />
              <zeebe:property name="inbound.responseExpression" value="={statusCode: 200, headers: {&#34;Content-Type&#34;: &#34;application/json&#34;}, body: {jsonrpc: &#34;2.0&#34;, id: request.body.id, result: {task: {id: (if request.body.params.message.taskId != null then request.body.params.message.taskId else request.body.params.message.messageId), contextId: (if request.body.params.message.contextId != null then request.body.params.message.contextId else (if request.body.params.message.taskId != null then request.body.params.message.taskId else request.body.params.message.messageId)), status: {state: if request.body.params.message.taskId != null then &#34;TASK_STATE_WORKING&#34; else &#34;TASK_STATE_SUBMITTED&#34;}}}}}" />
              <zeebe:property name="activationCondition" value="=request.body.method = &#34;SendMessage&#34; and request.body.params.message.messageId != null and request.body.params.message.taskId != null" />
              <zeebe:property name="correlationKeyExpression" value="=request.body.params.message.taskId" />
              <zeebe:property name="messageIdExpression" value="=request.body.params.message.messageId" />
              <zeebe:property name="resultExpression" value="={toolCallResult: string join(for part in request.body.params.message.parts return if part.text != null then part.text else &#34;&#34;, &#34; &#34;), messageText: string join(for part in request.body.params.message.parts return if part.text != null then part.text else &#34;&#34;, &#34; &#34;), pushNotification: request.body.params.configuration.taskPushNotificationConfig}" />
            </zeebe:properties>
          </bpmn:extensionElements>
          <bpmn:incoming>Flow_1kgyvmc</bpmn:incoming>
          <bpmn:messageEventDefinition id="MessageEventDefinition_0lbpu7p" messageRef="Message_0iqkhta" />
        </bpmn:intermediateCatchEvent>
        <bpmn:intermediateThrowEvent id="Server_PushNotification" name="Push task update to client" zeebe:modelerTemplate="dev.hansel.a2a.server.push.v1" zeebe:modelerTemplateVersion="2" zeebe:modelerTemplateIcon="data:image/svg+xml;base64,">
          <bpmn:documentation>Send a task update to the A2A client. Use TASK_STATE_INPUT_REQUIRED with a clarifying question when the request is ambiguous (the result is the client's answer), TASK_STATE_COMPLETED with the final answer, or TASK_STATE_FAILED with the reason.</bpmn:documentation>
          <bpmn:extensionElements>
            <zeebe:taskDefinition type="io.camunda:http-json:1" retries="3" />
            <zeebe:ioMapping>
              <zeebe:input source="=pushNotification.url" target="baseUrl" />
              <zeebe:input source="noAuth" target="authType" />
              <zeebe:input source="noAuth" target="authentication.type" />
              <zeebe:input source="pushTaskUpdate" target="operationId" />
              <zeebe:input source="=&#34;&#34;" target="operationPath" />
              <zeebe:input source="={}" target="queryParameters" />
              <zeebe:input source="POST" target="method" />
              <zeebe:input source="=fromAi(toolCall.state, &#34;TASK_STATE_INPUT_REQUIRED to ask the client a clarifying question, TASK_STATE_COMPLETED to deliver the final answer, TASK_STATE_FAILED if you cannot help.&#34;, &#34;string&#34;, {enum: [&#34;TASK_STATE_INPUT_REQUIRED&#34;, &#34;TASK_STATE_COMPLETED&#34;, &#34;TASK_STATE_FAILED&#34;]})" target="state" />
              <zeebe:input source="=fromAi(toolCall.text, &#34;The clarifying question or the final answer for the client.&#34;)" target="text" />
              <zeebe:input source="=taskId" target="taskId" />
              <zeebe:input source="=contextId" target="contextId" />
              <zeebe:input source="={task: {id: taskId, contextId: contextId, status: {state: state, message: {messageId: string(uuid()), role: &#34;ROLE_AGENT&#34;, parts: [{text: text}], taskId: taskId, contextId: contextId}}}}" target="body" />
              <zeebe:input source="= baseUrl + operationPath" target="url" />
              <zeebe:input source="=pushNotification.token" target="pushToken" />
              <zeebe:input source="={&#34;Content-Type&#34;: &#34;application/json&#34;, &#34;X-A2A-Notification-Token&#34;: pushToken}" target="headers" />
            </zeebe:ioMapping>
            <zeebe:taskHeaders>
              <zeebe:header key="resultExpression" value="={a2aPushStatus: response.status}" />
              <zeebe:header key="retryBackoff" value="PT30S" />
            </zeebe:taskHeaders>
          </bpmn:extensionElements>
          <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_1c5cs9r</bpmn:outgoing>
          <bpmn:messageEventDefinition id="MessageEventDefinition_0a8ma1x" />
        </bpmn:intermediateThrowEvent>
      </bpmn:adHocSubProcess>
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_08f6dbl" sourceRef="Server_MessageReceived" targetRef="Activity_10vg0yz" />
      <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Gateway_0oexjso" name="Final task state?" default="Flow_1dq5r6k">
        <bpmn:incoming>Flow_1vp49c3</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_1ilfuph</bpmn:outgoing>
        <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_0gbuh2v</bpmn:outgoing>
        <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_1x8ttwi</bpmn:outgoing>
        <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_1dq5r6k</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="Server_End" name="Task completed">
        <bpmn:incoming>Flow_1ilfuph</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="Event_0qrssbs" name="Task unknown">
        <bpmn:incoming>Flow_1dq5r6k</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="Event_00drhwt" name="Task canceled">
        <bpmn:incoming>Flow_1x8ttwi</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="Event_1l0zugo" name="Task failed">
        <bpmn:incoming>Flow_0gbuh2v</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_1ilfuph" name="completed" sourceRef="Gateway_0oexjso" targetRef="Server_End">
        <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">=taskState = "TASK_STATE_COMPLETED"</bpmn:conditionExpression>
      </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_0gbuh2v" name="failed" sourceRef="Gateway_0oexjso" targetRef="Event_1l0zugo">
        <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">=taskState = "TASK_STATE_FAILED"</bpmn:conditionExpression>
      </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_1x8ttwi" name="canceled" sourceRef="Gateway_0oexjso" targetRef="Event_00drhwt">
        <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">=taskState = "TASK_STATE_CANCELED"</bpmn:conditionExpression>
      </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_1dq5r6k" name="other" sourceRef="Gateway_0oexjso" targetRef="Event_0qrssbs" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_1vp49c3" sourceRef="Activity_10vg0yz" targetRef="Gateway_0oexjso" />
      <bpmn:startEvent id="Server_MessageReceived" name="A2A task received" zeebe:modelerTemplate="dev.hansel.a2a.server.send-message.v1" zeebe:modelerTemplateVersion="1" zeebe:modelerTemplateIcon="data:image/svg+xml;base64," isInterrupting="false">
        <bpmn:documentation>A2A 1.0 JSON-RPC SendMessage endpoint. A new task starts this instance; the HTTP response is the Task in TASK_STATE_SUBMITTED. taskId, contextId, messageText and the client's push notification config become process variables.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:extensionElements>
          <zeebe:properties>
            <zeebe:property name="inbound.type" value="io.camunda:webhook:1" />
            <zeebe:property name="inbound.shouldValidateHmac" value="disabled" />
            <zeebe:property name="inbound.auth.type" value="NONE" />
            <zeebe:property name="synchronousResponse" value="false" />
            <zeebe:property name="consumeUnmatchedEvents" value="true" />
            <zeebe:property name="deduplicationModeManualFlag" value="false" />
            <zeebe:property name="deduplicationMode" value="AUTO" />
            <zeebe:property name="inbound.method" value="post" />
            <zeebe:property name="inbound.context" value="a2a-server" />
            <zeebe:property name="inbound.verificationExpression" value="=if request.body.method = &#34;SendMessage&#34; and request.body.params.message.messageId != null then null else {statusCode: 200, headers: {&#34;Content-Type&#34;: &#34;application/json&#34;}, body: if request.body.method != &#34;SendMessage&#34; then {jsonrpc: &#34;2.0&#34;, id: request.body.id, error: {code: -32601, message: &#34;Method not found&#34;}} else {jsonrpc: &#34;2.0&#34;, id: request.body.id, error: {code: -32602, message: &#34;Invalid params: message.messageId is required&#34;}}}" />
            <zeebe:property name="inbound.responseExpression" value="={statusCode: 200, headers: {&#34;Content-Type&#34;: &#34;application/json&#34;}, body: {jsonrpc: &#34;2.0&#34;, id: request.body.id, result: {task: {id: (if request.body.params.message.taskId != null then request.body.params.message.taskId else request.body.params.message.messageId), contextId: (if request.body.params.message.contextId != null then request.body.params.message.contextId else (if request.body.params.message.taskId != null then request.body.params.message.taskId else request.body.params.message.messageId)), status: {state: if request.body.params.message.taskId != null then &#34;TASK_STATE_WORKING&#34; else &#34;TASK_STATE_SUBMITTED&#34;}}}}}" />
            <zeebe:property name="activationCondition" value="=request.body.method = &#34;SendMessage&#34; and request.body.params.message.messageId != null and request.body.params.message.taskId = null" />
            <zeebe:property name="correlationRequired" value="required" />
            <zeebe:property name="correlationKeyExpression" value="=request.params.agent" />
            <zeebe:property name="messageIdExpression" value="=request.body.params.message.messageId" />
            <zeebe:property name="resultExpression" value="={taskId: (if request.body.params.message.taskId != null then request.body.params.message.taskId else request.body.params.message.messageId), contextId: (if request.body.params.message.contextId != null then request.body.params.message.contextId else (if request.body.params.message.taskId != null then request.body.params.message.taskId else request.body.params.message.messageId)), messageText: string join(for part in request.body.params.message.parts return if part.text != null then part.text else &#34;&#34;, &#34; &#34;), pushNotification: request.body.params.configuration.taskPushNotificationConfig, taskState: &#34;TASK_STATE_SUBMITTED&#34;}" />
